# Every environment variable the API reads, with its default.
#
# Each line is commented out and shows the default the code uses; an empty
# value means there is no default. To change a setting when running with
# docker compose, copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and uncomment the lines
# you want: compose passes them to the API. compose.yaml always sets
# UPSTREAM_URL and FLAGS_URL itself, to wire the API to the mock and flagd
# containers. Outside compose, export the variables in your shell instead.
#
# A test (cmd/api/envexample_test.go) checks this file against the code and the
# README's Configuration table: same variables, same defaults.

# Base URL of the items upstream. Required, no default. May include a path
# prefix, but no query string or fragment.
# UPSTREAM_URL=

# Timeout for each upstream request.
# UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT=5s

# flagd OFREP base URL, e.g. http://flagd:8016. Unset disables flags.
# FLAGS_URL=

# Timeout for each flag evaluation.
# FLAGS_TIMEOUT=500ms

# A flagd-format flag file whose defaults replace the embedded flagd/flags.json.
# FLAGS_FALLBACK_FILE=

# Listen address. Takes precedence over PORT.
# ADDR=:8080

# Listen port, used only when ADDR is unset.
# PORT=

# debug, info, warn or error.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# json or text.
# LOG_FORMAT=json

# How long in-flight requests get to finish on SIGTERM.
# SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=10s

# enforce rejects requests that break a header rule; report only logs them.
# HEADER_GUARD_MODE=enforce

# The most request headers allowed (1 to 1048576).
# HEADER_MAX_COUNT=100

# The largest any one request header may be, name and value, in bytes.
# HEADER_MAX_BYTES=8192

# The largest the request headers may be in total, in bytes.
# HEADER_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=32768
